   1385  feff							; LaserHitTestBody — MOVED from bank0 (S5.4, entry tramp $FE86 -> `jmp $FF00`).
   1386  feff							; Contact-missile kill (redesign 2026-10-08): CollisionX = LaserX (cur M0
   1387  feff							; arg, stored by LaserInput .LaserGo), drawn M0 = [A-7, A]. The body tests
   1388  feff							; ONE tip cell for wall first, then the missile's OWN body box against each
   1389  feff							; live enemy — no piercing: first contact wins and the caller resets the
   1390  feff							; beam to the eye. Vertical: beam rows [RoomY+2, RoomY+3] vs enemy [Y,+7] ->
   1391  feff							; (RoomY-Y)+3 in [0..8]. Horizontal (same convention as CheckEnemyHit):
   1392  feff							; |eLo-lo| <= 7 via (d+7) in [0..14]; caller keeps arg in [0,159].
   1393  feff							; Fold-free: enemy records are level data in THIS bank — stage once, direct
   1394  feff							; `lda (FetchPtr),Y` for the type (was `jsr FoldIndirect`).
   1395  feff							; RESULT PROTOCOL (pads cannot nest from a pad body — the kill/lamp/wall
   1396  feff							; ACTIONS stay in bank0's LaserInput): every exit returns A + Z through
   1397  feff							; ReturnPad (sta/rts preserve both): A=0 no contact (keep travelling) /
   1398  feff							; #$50 kill (dead bit set here, caller scores + resets) / A=1 lamp (caller
   1399  feff							; does CallPad_SetRoomDark + resets) / A=2 wall tip (caller resets, no
   1400  feff							; score). First live enemy in span only (dead mask skips it next frame —
   1401  feff							; no resurrection, no double score).
   1402  feff							; Does NOT touch Temp (joystick still live at the call site).
   1403  feff							; Wall first: the body tail-jmps to LaserWallClamp ($F25A) — tip cell
   1404  feff							; (patch-strip + mirrored PF rows) — solid returns A=2 straight through
   1405  feff							; ReturnPad (enemies behind the wall survive); clear ends
   1406  feff							; `jmp LaserClampDone` (back here = enemy loop): stack depth unchanged.
   1407  feff							; Clobbers A/X/Y/FetchPtr + CollisionCellY/CollisionEndY, RectCount,
   1408  feff							; CollisionEndX (strip marker); MODIFIES NOTHING else (no clamp any more).
